		{"id":"59c875b8e9ed0a64","type":"text","text":"**Procedural modeling** of phenomenological fuzzy objects: \n* particle advection by volume vector field\n\nExample:\n1. Mesh is used to generate main shape (only surface).\n2. Differential geometry OPs are used to compute information per surface points (e.g., tangent field)\n3. Surface is rasterized into volume grid where each cell is assigned with vector value\n4. Particle simulation is using volume grid information for movement.\n\nExample:\n1. Mesh is used to generate main shape (only surface).\n2. Mesh is rasterized: converted to grid\n3. Noise is computed for each grid cell resulting in volume vector field\n4. Particle simulation is using volume grid information for movement.","x":-3160,"y":2485,"width":620,"height":502},
		{"id":"2521614d04388988","type":"file","file":"Images/Fuzzy/LectureExamples/6/InitialGeometry.jpg","x":-6933,"y":3396,"width":400,"height":233},
		{"id":"46f0fbcf35151d85","type":"file","file":"Images/Fuzzy/LectureExamples/6/VolumesParticles2.jpg","x":-4883,"y":3227,"width":400,"height":247},
		{"id":"9737fbea700a8ddc","type":"text","text":"Useful for:\n* Custom vector fields\n* Phenomenological fluid simulation\n\t* https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/sop/volumerasterize.html","x":-4463,"y":3248,"width":380,"height":204},
		{"id":"b78dada2ae1751fc","type":"link","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rC9EGQJOLyE","x":-3905,"y":2597,"width":640,"height":360},
		{"id":"a17a57a394b8d1e7","type":"link","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WKDY5b_V5go","x":-3905,"y":3022,"width":640,"height":360},
		{"id":"710fa593121a4305","type":"text","text":"Point Cloud Open and Point Cloud Filter VOP/VEX nodes/functions are used to access point information around current particle in POP VOP. This way, vector field stored at points can be used to drive particles.\n\nIt can be used for any kind of points in surface or volume:\n1. Surface points: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zJls__AJlJo\n2. Volume points: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JS3rw7W1gN4&t=11s ","x":-3160,"y":3068,"width":724,"height":314},
		{"id":"e105bd1efe59fb2c","type":"text","text":"Particle-based fluid simulation approaches:\n* SPH \n* PSD\n* FLIP\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Bx_D_51bF7Y","x":-3160,"y":3422,"width":724,"height":200},
		{"id":"709903a13b61cd40","type":"text","text":"Empty Volume","x":-5802,"y":2880,"width":250,"height":60},
